<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Funds acquire 10 pct of RAI share capital.</title>
<headline>Funds acquire 10 pct of RAI share capital.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Real Africa Investments (RAI) said on Monday the Public Investment Commissioners had acquired 10 percent of the issued share capital held by the South African Clothing and Textile Workers' Union.</p>
<p>The union's shareholding in RAI had been reduced to 1.5 percent, the group said.</p>
<p>The Public Investment Commissioners represent a wide spread of pension funds.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
